# Copy to .env (git-ignored) and fill in locally. Never commit .env.
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GET YOUR FREE NASA API KEY HERE:  https://api.nasa.gov
#   (the "Generate API Key" form:   https://api.nasa.gov/#signUp)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# NASA API key: each team member uses their OWN free key.
#   1. Open https://api.nasa.gov and scroll to "Generate API Key"
#   2. Fill in the form (first name, last name, email); the key is emailed
#      to you instantly. No special NASA Space Apps key is needed.
#   3. Paste it below, after the "=", with no quotes or spaces.
# Rate limits: a personal key allows 1,000 requests/hour across all
# api.nasa.gov APIs. Until you have one, NASA's public DEMO_KEY works for light
# testing (30 requests/hour and 50/day per IP). Lost key: https://api.nasa.gov/#recovery
#
# Related NASA platforms (no key needed for these):
#   https://data.nasa.gov        open datasets
#   https://earthdata.nasa.gov   Earth observation data (needs an Earthdata login, not this key)
#   https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov     JPL Horizons and solar-system APIs
#   https://trek.nasa.gov/moon   Moon Trek maps and tiles
#
# Rules: backend/server use only. Never expose it to the frontend (no VITE_
# prefix), never commit .env, never paste the key into issues, PRs or chat.
# Used by: src/acquire/space_weather.py (NASA DONKI space-weather context via
# src/acquire/nasa_api.py). The core engine (SPICE, LOLA, PGDA, Horizons) needs
# no key. If NASA_API_KEY is empty, scripts fall back to DEMO_KEY.
NASA_API_KEY=

# Backend (FastAPI, backend/core/config.py reads .env from the repo root)
# OFFLINE=0
# CORS_ORIGINS=https://apolloharness.web.app,https://apolloharness.firebaseapp.com,http://localhost:5173
